 "about_text": "David Kordansky Gallery is a contemporary art gallery founded in 2003 in Los Angeles's Chinatown neighborhood as an incubator for emerging artists. It moved to Culver City in 2008 and now operates a 20,000-square-foot campus in Mid-City Los Angeles, alongside a 5,000-square-foot space in Chelsea, New York. The Los Angeles site comprises three exhibition spaces across two buildings with a courtyard, allowing simultaneous shows and programming that includes performance, film, and outdoor sculpture. The gallery represents artists working across all media, emphasizing individuality over a shared aesthetic, and situates its program within the history of postwar Los Angeles art while engaging global contemporary practice. It regularly participates in major international art fairs and produces exhibition catalogues and artist's books.",
